  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-1076497" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sense International</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TO20 Promoting Inclusive Early Childhood Development Education (ECDE) in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Working through government structures and with civil society, we will demonstrate affordable contextually-appropriate &#x2013; and hence scalable and sustainable &#x2013;  inclusive Early Childhood Development Education (ECDE) approaches for children with disabilities in selected pre-primary schools in Nyanza Region, Homa Bay, Kenya. The innovation is aiming to test which low cost strategies work well in ECDE settings and how girls and boys with disabilities can be supported to attend pre-primary school within their local setting. Strategies to enable children with multiple and complex disabilities to access an early education will be explored, including the use of home based care. Sense International Will have a focus around complex disabilities and homebased education and will collaborate on advising about working with parents and guardians to strengthen the home based support system with the aim of supporting them to transit to inclusive education and into mainstream schools.</narrative>
  </description>
